# Set default behavior to automatically normalize line endings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Migrate binary files to GIT LFS
*.jpeg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.gif filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Archives
*.[zZ][iI][pP] binary
*.[tT][aA][rR] binary
*.[tT][aA][rR].[gG][zZ] binary
*.[tT][aA][rR].[bB][zZ] binary
*.[tT][aA][rR].[xX][zZ] binary

# Generated third-party notice: reproduces upstream license files verbatim,
# some of which use CRLF. Without `-text` the `* text=auto eol=lf` rule above
# rewrites them to LF on checkout while `cargo about` keeps re-rendering CRLF,
# so `task rust:license:notice:check` would fail on every fresh clone.
LICENSE-THIRD-PARTY.md -text

# OCX lock files
ocx.lock merge=union

# Bazel's module lockfile. A line-based merge driver (`union`, `ours`)
# interleaves or duplicates a digest key WITHOUT writing a conflict marker,
# which also defeats Bazel's own conflict detector — it looks for `<<<<<<<` in
# the text. A silent bad merge is strictly worse than a visible one, so this
# file gets Bazel's JSON-aware driver and nothing else does: pointed at a
# foreign lockfile it parses a schema it was not written for.
#
# The driver name still needs a one-time registration per clone and per CI
# runner (`git config merge.bazel-lockfile-merge.driver ...`); until then git
# falls back to a plain text merge, which conflicts loudly rather than
# corrupting quietly.
#
# No task registers it, and that is not an oversight: **the driver program is
# not in this tree and the pinned binary does not carry one.** Measured on
# 9.2.0 — `bazel help mod` lists no `merge-lockfile` subcommand, and the
# install base ships no `*lockfile*` script. Upstream's driver is
# `scripts/bazel-lockfile-merge.py` in the bazelbuild/bazel *repository*, so
# registering it means vendoring a JSON merge driver for someone else's schema
# (`quality-core.md` § Don't Own Non-Domain Code) or depending on a checkout
# nobody here has. The loud text-merge conflict is the accepted state until a
# release ships the driver with the binary.
MODULE.bazel.lock merge=bazel-lockfile-merge
